0 // After LEGO Education's building instructions for Driving Base 1, steps
0 // 1 to 25, leaving out the cables, cable clips and small connectors.
0 // The origin is the middle of the axle on the table; forward is -z, so
0 // the robot's left is +x, and y points down, as in all LDraw files. The
0 // wheels (39367p01) go on the motors' outputs at (140, -70, 0) on the left
0 // and (-140, -70, 0) on the right: see scene.py.

0 // Step 1: the frame, under the motors
1 26 0 -30 60 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 39794.dat

0 // Step 3: the motors, outputs outwards, cables at the back
1 15 -40 -70 0 0 1 0 -1 0 0 0 0 1 54696p01.dat
1 15 40 -70 0 0 -1 0 1 0 0 0 0 1 54696p01.dat

0 // Step 4: the axles in the motors' outputs
1 14 -120 -70 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 4519.dat
1 14 120 -70 0 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 4519.dat

0 // Step 14: the hub on top of the motors
1 15 0 -100 80 -1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 -1 45601c01.dat

0 // Steps 10 to 13: the ball caster under the back of the hub
1 26 0 -110 175 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 39793.dat
1 322 0 -70 180 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 39370c01.dat

0 // Steps 15 to 21: the beams along the sides
1 0 -100 -110 40 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 32278.dat
1 0 100 -110 40 1 0 0 0 1 0 0 0 1 32278.dat
